{"id": "c1f9169b-dbae-4cf1-83de-d17948b9e102", "slug": "vertexa-build-beyond-the-ordinary-1", "title": "Vertexa - Build Beyond the Ordinary", "description": "Vertexa Build CTA Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-staff-featured-2026-05-22\"\nname: \"Vertexa - Build Beyond the Ordinary\"\ndescription: \"Vertexa Build CTA Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#2C40FF\"\n  secondary: \"#02040A\"\n  accent: \"#4A60FF\"\n  background: \"#02040A\"\n  surface: \"#18181B\"\n  text-primary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-secondary: \"#A1A1AA\"\n  border: \"#27272A\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# Vertexa - Build Beyond the Ordinary\nSource: Neuform staff featured templates. Author: Sourasith Phomhome (@madebysourasith). Views: 134; favorites: 6; remixes: 3.\nTags: cta, animated, webgl, threejs, navigation, links, support, action.\n## Overview\nVertexa Build CTA Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.\n\nVertexa Products Solutions Resources Company Get Started Build Beyond the Ordinary. We build scalable digital products and experiences that help ambitious companies grow faster. Get Started\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Build Beyond the Ordinary..\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #2C40FF, secondary #02040A, accent #4A60FF, background #02040A, surface #18181B, text-primary #FFFFFF. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Inter for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nAuthentication and CTA controls should preserve the source button hierarchy, input density, and focused conversion path.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\" class=\"antialiased\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Vertexa - Build Beyond the Ordinary</title>\n\n    <!-- Tailwind CSS -->\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n\n    <!-- Iconify -->\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n\n    <!-- GSAP & ScrollTrigger -->\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js\"></script>\n\n    <!-- Tailwind Config for precise colors -->\n    <script>\n        tailwind.config = {\n            theme: {\n                extend: {\n                    colors: {\n                        'vertex-bg': '#02040a',\n                        'vertex-blue': '#2c40ff',\n                        'vertex-blue-bright': '#4a60ff',\n                    },\n                    fontFamily: {\n                        sans: ['Inter', 'system-ui', 'sans-serif'],\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    </script>\n</head>\n<body class=\"bg-vertex-bg text-white font-sans overflow-x-hidden selection:bg-vertex-blue selection:text-white relative min-h-screen\">\n\n    <!-- Canvas Background Layer -->\n    <div class=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 pointer-events-none overflow-hidden\" style=\"opacity: 0.85;\">\n        <canvas id=\"pixel-canvas\" class=\"absolute inset-0 w-full h-full\"></canvas>\n        <!-- CSS Scanline Overlay to match texture -->\n        <div class=\"absolute inset-0\" style=\"background: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, transparent 2px, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4) 2px, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4) 4px);\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Main Content Wrapper -->\n    <div class=\"relative z-10 flex flex-col min-h-screen\">\n\n        <!-- Header -->\n        <header class=\"w-full max-w-[90rem] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-12 py-6 flex justify-between items-center\">\n            <!-- Logo -->\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"flex items-center gap-2 group\">\n                <svg width=\"28\" height=\"28\" viewBox=\"0 0 32 32\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"transform group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-300\">\n                    <path d=\"M16 28L2 4H10L16 16L22 4H30L16 28Z\" fill=\"#2c40ff\"/>\n                    <path d=\"M16 28L8 12H16L20 20L16 28Z\" fill=\"#6b7cff\" fill-opacity=\"0.4\"/>\n                </svg>\n                <span class=\"text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight\">Vertexa</span>\n            </a>\n\n            <!-- Navigation -->\n            <nav class=\"hidden md:flex items-center gap-10\">\n                <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors\">Products</a>\n                <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors\">Solutions</a>\n                <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors\">Resources</a>\n                <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors\">Company</a>\n            </nav>\n\n            <!-- Header CTA -->\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"hidden sm:inline-flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-medium text-white border border-gray-700 hover:border-gray-400 rounded-md px-5 py-2 transition-all duration-300\">\n                Get Started\n            </a>\n        </header>\n\n        <!-- Hero Section -->\n        <main class=\"flex-1 w-full max-w-[90rem] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-12 flex items-center pt-10 pb-32\">\n            <div class=\"max-w-2xl relative z-10\">\n\n                <!-- Masked Reveal Title -->\n                <h1 id=\"hero-title\" class=\"text-6xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[1.1] mb-6\">\n                    <span style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; padding-bottom: 0.1em; margin-bottom: -0.1em;\">\n                        <span class=\"reveal-word block\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">Build</span>\n                    </span>\n                    <span style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; padding-bottom: 0.1em; margin-bottom: -0.1em;\">\n                        <span class=\"reveal-word block\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">Beyond</span>\n                    </span>\n                    <br class=\"hidden sm:block\" />\n                    <span style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; padding-bottom: 0.1em; margin-bottom: -0.1em;\">\n                        <span class=\"reveal-word block\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">the</span>\n                    </span>\n                    <span style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; padding-bottom: 0.1em; margin-bottom: -0.1em;\">\n                        <span class=\"reveal-word block text-vertex-blue\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">Ordinary.</span>\n                    </span>\n                </h1>\n\n                <!-- Subtitle -->\n                <p class=\"text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-400 max-w-lg leading-relaxed mb-10 opacity-0\" id=\"hero-desc\">\n                    We build scalable digital products and experiences that help ambitious companies grow faster.\n                </p>\n\n                <!-- CTA Button -->\n                <div class=\"opacity-0\" id=\"hero-cta\">\n                    <a href=\"#\" class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-vertex-blue hover:bg-vertex-blue-bright text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-md font-medium text-base transition-all duration-300 shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(44,64,255,0.3)] hover:shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(44,64,255,0.5)] group\">\n                        Get Started\n                        <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:arrow-right-up-linear\" class=\"text-xl transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5 group-hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-transform\"></iconify-icon>\n                    </a>\n                </div>\n\n            </div>\n        </main>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Application Logic -->\n    <script>\n        // --- 1. GSAP Animations ---\n        gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);\n\n        // Masked staggered word reveal for H1\n        gsap.to(\".reveal-word\", {\n            y: \"0%\",\n            duration: 1.2,\n            ease: \"power4.out\",\n            stagger: 0.15,\n            scrollTrigger: {\n                trigger: \"#hero-title\",\n                start: \"top 85%\",\n            }\n        });\n\n        // Fade in subtitle and CTA after title\n        gsap.to([\"#hero-desc\", \"#hero-cta\"], {\n            opacity: 1,\n            y: 0,\n            duration: 1,\n            ease: \"power3.out\",\n            stagger: 0.2,\n            delay: 0.6,\n            startAt: { y: 20 },\n            scrollTrigger: {\n                trigger: \"#hero-title\",\n                start: \"top 85%\",\n            }\n        });\n\n\n        // --- 2. Canvas Pixel Wave Effect ---\n        const canvas = document.getElementById('pixel-canvas');\n        const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d', { alpha: false }); // Optimize for solid background clearing\n\n        let width, height;\n        const blockSize = 28;\n        let blocks = [];\n\n        function resize() {\n            width = window.innerWidth;\n            height = window.innerHeight;\n            canvas.width = width;\n            canvas.height = height;\n            initBlocks();\n        }\n\n        function initBlocks() {\n            blocks = [];\n            const columns = Math.ceil(width / blockSize);\n            const rows = Math.ceil(height / blockSize);\n\n            for (let c = 0; c < columns; c++) {\n                // Determine structure shape: builds up from bottom right\n                let normalizedX = c / columns;\n                // Exponential curve to create the \"mountain\" effect on the right\n                let curve = Math.pow(normalizedX, 4);\n\n                // Base starting row based on curve\n                let startRow = rows - Math.floor(rows * curve * 0.9) - Math.floor(Math.random() * 4);\n\n                for (let r = 0; r < rows; r++) {\n                    let shouldAdd = false;\n                    let blockType = 'base'; // base, bright, sparse\n\n                    if (r >= startRow) {\n                        // Dense main body\n                        if (Math.random() > 0.05) shouldAdd = true;\n                    } else if (r >= startRow - 4 && normalizedX > 0.4) {\n                        // Jagged top edge\n                        if (Math.random() > 0.6) {\n                            shouldAdd = true;\n                            blockType = 'sparse';\n                        }\n                    } else if (normalizedX > 0.6 && Math.random() > 0.98) {\n                        // Floating particles high up\n                        shouldAdd = true;\n                        blockType = 'sparse';\n                    }\n\n                    if (shouldAdd) {\n                        // Assign colors matching reference\n                        let rColor = 0;\n                        let gColor = 0;\n                        let bColor = 255;\n                        let maxAlpha = 1;\n\n                        // Variation in blues\n                        let rand = Math.random();\n                        if (rand > 0.8) {\n                            // Bright cyan/blue\n                            rColor = 40; gColor = 80; bColor = 255;\n                        } else if (rand > 0.4) {\n                            // Pure blue\n                            rColor = 10; gColor = 20; bColor = 240;\n                        } else {\n                            // Darker navy\n                            rColor = 5; gColor = 10; bColor = 150;\n                            maxAlpha = 0.7;\n                        }\n\n                        if(blockType === 'sparse') maxAlpha *= 0.6;\n\n                        blocks.push({\n                            x: c * blockSize,\n                            y: r * blockSize,\n                            r: rColor,\n                            g: gColor,\n                            b: bColor,\n                            alpha: Math.random() * maxAlpha,\n                            targetAlpha: Math.random() * maxAlpha,\n                            maxAlpha: maxAlpha,\n                            speed: Math.random() * 0.02 + 0.005\n                        });\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        window.addEventListener('resize', resize);\n        resize(); // Initial call\n\n        function animate() {\n            // Fill background with dark color\n            ctx.fillStyle = '#02040a';\n            ctx.fillRect(0, 0, width, height);\n\n            blocks.forEach(b => {\n                // Flicker animation logic\n                b.alpha += (b.targetAlpha - b.alpha) * b.speed;\n\n                // Assign new target alpha when reached\n                if (Math.abs(b.alpha - b.targetAlpha) < 0.02) {\n                    b.targetAlpha = Math.random() * b.maxAlpha;\n                }\n\n                // Draw main block\n                ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${b.r}, ${b.g}, ${b.b}, ${b.alpha})`;\n                // -1 for slight gap between blocks\n                ctx.fillRect(b.x, b.y, blockSize - 1, blockSize - 1);\n\n                // Draw slight highlight on top edge to enhance blocky feel\n                ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(255, 255, 255, ${b.alpha * 0.15})`;\n                ctx.fillRect(b.x, b.y, blockSize - 1, 2);\n            });\n\n            requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n        }\n\n        animate();\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "vertexa-build-beyond-the-ordinary-1.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/staff-featured-2026-05-22/vertexa-build-beyond-the-ordinary-1.jpg", "source_name": "vertexa-build-beyond-the-ordinary-1-DESIGN.md", "views": 225, "forks": 5, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "5bd6211c-bd4c-467c-b442-4312cac4712c", "created_at": "2026-05-22T07:58:12.433844+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-03T11:23:51.563938+00:00"}